{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The resistor assortment and heat shrink tubing fit my breadboard, LED, battery-holder, and relay purchases because they help me build circuits and insulate their connections.",
    "Small bolts and nuts could help mount circuit boards, while test clips and hooks could help check connections, provided they fit my meter. These support the hands-on projects reflected in my history."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A CNC bit and a dedicated 3D printer controller require equipment and projects I have not shown a need for. Buying Arduino components does not mean I am working with either machine.",
    "The sharpening tool, red acrylic sheet, dispensing syringes, and drywall screws do not address a current task I recognize. Their usefulness depends on a specific project, material, or fastening need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in building small circuits seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop tool or fabrication supply.",
    "My caster purchase seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest general furniture fasteners, although it does not establish that I need drywall or wood screws."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The useful connection between my electronics purchases is their role in assembling, wiring, and testing small circuits. Supplies that serve those same tasks feel more relevant than another specialized controller.",
    "I buy when something fits a concrete need. Dimensions, electrical specifications, and compatibility matter, and my older electronics purchases do not confirm that every related project is still active."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical DIY interests but stretched them beyond small-circuit supplies into specialized tools and materials I have no current reason to buy."
}"}
